From: fllama (not yet upstream)
Subject: server : realtime context overflow aborts the process

A realtime conversation whose audio or text does not fit in the context
fails with ERROR_TYPE_EXCEED_CONTEXT_SIZE. send_error(slot, ...) passes the
slot's prompt tokens, which a realtime slot never has (0), and send_error
asserts n_prompt_tokens > 0 for that error type: GGML_ASSERT aborts the
whole app. Upstream master 9581154a2 (2026-11-17) has the same code. Drop
this patch when llama.cpp fixes it.
---
diff --git a/tools/server/server-context.cpp b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
index 78c8ef14..1fcc51c8 100644
--- a/tools/server/server-context.cpp
+++ b/tools/server/server-context.cpp
@@ -3692,7 +3692,8 @@ private:
                 return;
             }
             if (!slot.rt->update()) {
-                send_error(slot, slot.rt->error, slot.rt->error_type);
+                // the conversation has no prompt tokens: a full context is the context size
+                send_error(slot.task->id, slot.rt->error, slot.rt->error_type, slot.n_ctx, slot.n_ctx);
                 slot.release();
                 return;
             }
